I can't explain the screenshot of the LOD profile output. When you have linked QTL, the LOD profiles for the two QTL will both cover the interval between them, so you'll have a stretch of the chromosome repeated.

When you have a very strong QTL, haley-knott regression can give apparent evidence for two tightly-linked QTL. You might try the multiple imputation method.

karl

